1
00:00:00,306 --> 00:00:02,194
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,633 --> 00:00:04,602
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,204
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,204 --> 00:00:08,836
I've been a paramedic for
twenty-two years.

5
00:00:08,836 --> 00:00:10,173
Kneeling on roadsides

6
00:00:10,173 --> 00:00:11,989
and kitchen floors next to
patients,

7
00:00:12,479 --> 00:00:14,673
carrying stretchers up and
down stairs,

8
00:00:14,673 --> 00:00:15,469
climbing in and out

9
00:00:15,469 --> 00:00:16,315
of the back of the rig

10
00:00:16,703 --> 00:00:18,111
more times than I could
ever count.

11
00:00:19,091 --> 00:00:20,162
That's a lot of years

12
00:00:20,162 --> 00:00:21,366
on a pair of knees.

13
00:00:21,366 --> 00:00:22,223
I had my right knee

14
00:00:22,223 --> 00:00:23,695
replaced two years ago.

15
00:00:23,695 --> 00:00:25,510
It has hurt every day
since.

16
00:00:25,510 --> 00:00:26,854
Not surgery pain.

17
00:00:26,854 --> 00:00:28,038
I know what that felt
like,

18
00:00:28,038 --> 00:00:28,891
and it went away.

19
00:00:28,891 --> 00:00:29,803
This is different.

20
00:00:30,164 --> 00:00:30,977
Tight.

21
00:00:30,977 --> 00:00:31,418
Full.

22
00:00:31,879 --> 00:00:32,772
Like a band around

23
00:00:32,772 --> 00:00:34,568
the joint that never
loosens.

24
00:00:34,568 --> 00:00:35,771
And for two years

25
00:00:35,771 --> 00:00:37,396
I've been told the same
thing.

26
00:00:37,396 --> 00:00:38,098
Give it time.

27
00:00:38,529 --> 00:00:39,994
At six weeks it was
swelling,

28
00:00:39,994 --> 00:00:41,298
and swelling is normal.

29
00:00:41,298 --> 00:00:42,301
At three months,

30
00:00:42,301 --> 00:00:43,454
give it six.

31
00:00:43,454 --> 00:00:44,166
At six months,

32
00:00:44,166 --> 00:00:45,791
some knees take a full
year.

33
00:00:45,791 --> 00:00:46,493
At a year,

34
00:00:46,493 --> 00:00:48,158
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

35
00:00:48,901 --> 00:00:49,914
And I didn't just wait.

36
00:00:50,455 --> 00:00:52,030
We went down the list.

37
00:00:52,030 --> 00:00:53,424
More physical therapy.

38
00:00:53,424 --> 00:00:54,287
Every session,

39
00:00:54,287 --> 00:00:55,571
every exercise at home.

40
00:00:55,952 --> 00:00:57,115
I got stronger.

41
00:00:57,115 --> 00:00:58,439
The tightness never moved.

42
00:00:58,820 --> 00:01:00,134
The pain pills helped,

43
00:01:00,134 --> 00:01:01,147
and that was the problem.

44
00:01:01,559 --> 00:01:03,504
I'm already on enough
every morning,

45
00:01:03,504 --> 00:01:04,487
and nobody could tell me

46
00:01:04,487 --> 00:01:05,480
when I'd get to stop.

47
00:01:06,012 --> 00:01:07,246
Then a nerve block.

48
00:01:07,246 --> 00:01:08,941
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

49
00:01:08,941 --> 00:01:10,255
And after that, a second

50
00:01:10,255 --> 00:01:11,348
operation to go back

51
00:01:11,348 --> 00:01:12,562
in and do it over.

52
00:01:12,953 --> 00:01:13,655
I said no.

53
00:01:14,016 --> 00:01:15,935
Every morning I pulled on
my uniform

54
00:01:15,935 --> 00:01:16,873
and my knee felt like

55
00:01:16,873 --> 00:01:18,424
a band was wrapped around
it,

56
00:01:18,424 --> 00:01:20,455
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

57
00:01:21,373 --> 00:01:22,995
Every morning I took
something for it

58
00:01:22,995 --> 00:01:24,484
and went in for my shift.

59
00:01:24,484 --> 00:01:26,048
Couldn't do the stairs,

60
00:01:26,048 --> 00:01:27,131
couldn't stand at the
counter

61
00:01:27,131 --> 00:01:28,696
long enough to finish
dinner,

62
00:01:28,696 --> 00:01:30,231
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

63
00:01:30,231 --> 00:01:32,598
game without shifting
every two minutes.

64
00:01:32,598 --> 00:01:33,681
It woke me at night,

65
00:01:34,072 --> 00:01:35,978
and it turned ordinary
things,

66
00:01:36,459 --> 00:01:38,084
like getting in the car

67
00:01:38,084 --> 00:01:39,669
or up off the couch,

68
00:01:39,669 --> 00:01:40,803
into a decision.

69
00:01:40,803 --> 00:01:42,116
After a long and serious

70
00:01:42,116 --> 00:01:43,430
talk with my wife,

71
00:01:43,430 --> 00:01:45,045
I went back in one more
time.

72
00:01:45,667 --> 00:01:46,821
That was the fourth set

73
00:01:46,821 --> 00:01:48,325
of X-rays on this knee.

74
00:01:48,716 --> 00:01:50,000
And like the three before
it,

75
00:01:50,401 --> 00:01:52,869
the answer was everything
looks great.

76
00:01:52,869 --> 00:01:54,594
No loosening, no
infection,

77
00:01:54,594 --> 00:01:55,156
nothing wrong.

78
00:01:55,617 --> 00:01:56,460
Only this time there

79
00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:57,442
was no new number.

80
00:01:57,864 --> 00:01:58,937
Nobody said

81
00:01:58,937 --> 00:02:00,211
give it another six
months.

82
00:02:00,211 --> 00:02:01,625
There was nothing left to
give it.

83
00:02:02,086 --> 00:02:02,899
I sat in the parking

84
00:02:02,899 --> 00:02:03,611
lot for a while.

85
00:02:04,153 --> 00:02:05,216
Okay, I thought.

86
00:02:05,667 --> 00:02:06,740
Then explain this.

87
00:02:07,262 --> 00:02:09,148
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

88
00:02:09,148 --> 00:02:10,585
I hit my breaking point.

89
00:02:10,585 --> 00:02:12,207
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

90
00:02:12,799 --> 00:02:13,748
I'd just come home off

91
00:02:13,748 --> 00:02:14,686
a long night shift.

92
00:02:15,135 --> 00:02:16,697
Everyone in the house was
asleep

93
00:02:17,299 --> 00:02:19,503
and I was downstairs in
the recliner,

94
00:02:19,503 --> 00:02:21,043
still in my uniform,

95
00:02:21,043 --> 00:02:22,359
with my leg up,

96
00:02:22,359 --> 00:02:23,931
trying to find any angle

97
00:02:23,931 --> 00:02:25,431
where it didn't feel like
something

98
00:02:25,431 --> 00:02:27,614
was wrapped around my knee
and tightening.

99
00:02:27,965 --> 00:02:29,951
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

100
00:02:30,302 --> 00:02:31,876
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

101
00:02:32,518 --> 00:02:33,481
And I just thought,

102
00:02:33,481 --> 00:02:35,287
is this really my life
now?

103
00:02:35,287 --> 00:02:36,621
I can't live like this.

104
00:02:37,032 --> 00:02:38,938
So I made myself a
promise.

105
00:02:38,938 --> 00:02:39,790
I wouldn't go a day

106
00:02:39,790 --> 00:02:41,104
without looking for an
answer.

107
00:02:41,596 --> 00:02:42,759
And when I found one,

108
00:02:43,190 --> 00:02:45,076
I'd share it with everyone

109
00:02:45,076 --> 00:02:46,270
going through the same
thing.

110
00:02:46,972 --> 00:02:48,085
So I got my laptop

111
00:02:48,085 --> 00:02:49,479
out and went looking.

112
00:02:50,001 --> 00:02:51,014
Not for a product.

113
00:02:51,365 --> 00:02:52,368
For an explanation.

114
00:02:52,879 --> 00:02:54,565
Mayo Clinic forums,

115
00:02:54,565 --> 00:02:56,681
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

116
00:02:56,681 --> 00:02:59,349
doctor videos, medical
animations.

117
00:02:59,349 --> 00:03:00,282
And that's when I found

118
00:03:00,282 --> 00:03:02,087
a video from a physical
therapist

119
00:03:02,087 --> 00:03:02,619
named Dr.

120
00:03:02,619 --> 00:03:04,635
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

121
00:03:04,635 --> 00:03:06,330
had been through exactly
this.

122
00:03:06,681 --> 00:03:08,867
But before I say anything
else,

123
00:03:08,867 --> 00:03:10,282
I want to be straight with
you.

124
00:03:10,673 --> 00:03:13,080
You've already had
something work fast.

125
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:14,023
The ice.

126
00:03:14,023 --> 00:03:15,658
The first week of a new
pill.

127
00:03:15,658 --> 00:03:17,584
The good day after a
session.

128
00:03:17,584 --> 00:03:18,677
Then it wore off.

129
00:03:18,677 --> 00:03:20,783
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

130
00:03:21,285 --> 00:03:23,401
Fast relief isn't relief.

131
00:03:23,401 --> 00:03:24,244
It's a preview.

132
00:03:24,715 --> 00:03:25,738
So I'm not going to tell

133
00:03:25,738 --> 00:03:27,192
you this works fast.

134
00:03:27,192 --> 00:03:27,925
It doesn't.

135
00:03:28,406 --> 00:03:30,242
But if you're willing to
be patient,

136
00:03:30,242 --> 00:03:30,974
and to look at what's

137
00:03:30,974 --> 00:03:32,268
going on around your new
knee

138
00:03:32,268 --> 00:03:33,872
instead of inside it,
there

139
00:03:33,872 --> 00:03:35,728
is a real reason it still
hurts.

140
00:03:36,089 --> 00:03:37,544
And something you can do
about it.

141
00:03:38,416 --> 00:03:39,720
Let me explain what he
said,

142
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:41,154
because this is what
changed

143
00:03:41,154 --> 00:03:42,157
everything for me.

144
00:03:42,609 --> 00:03:44,203
He started with the
basics.

145
00:03:44,705 --> 00:03:46,210
A knee replacement takes
out

146
00:03:46,210 --> 00:03:47,955
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

147
00:03:47,955 --> 00:03:49,369
in metal and plastic.

148
00:03:49,369 --> 00:03:51,395
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

149
00:03:51,395 --> 00:03:52,759
you had before the
operation.

150
00:03:53,221 --> 00:03:54,354
That part I already knew.

151
00:03:54,886 --> 00:03:56,230
But then he explained
something

152
00:03:56,230 --> 00:03:57,604
nobody had ever told me.

153
00:03:57,604 --> 00:03:58,025
He said,

154
00:03:58,426 --> 00:04:00,121
think about a swollen foot

155
00:04:00,121 --> 00:04:01,014
inside a shoe.

156
00:04:01,816 --> 00:04:02,870
The shoe didn't shrink.

157
00:04:03,241 --> 00:04:05,006
Your foot is taking up
more room,

158
00:04:05,437 --> 00:04:06,872
so everything feels
cramped

159
00:04:06,872 --> 00:04:08,065
and tight and squeezed.

160
00:04:08,486 --> 00:04:09,379
Your new knee sits

161
00:04:09,379 --> 00:04:10,894
in a limited space with
living

162
00:04:10,894 --> 00:04:12,539
tissue packed all around
it.

163
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:14,805
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

164
00:04:14,805 --> 00:04:16,210
had to work through that
tissue.

165
00:04:16,641 --> 00:04:18,948
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

166
00:04:19,530 --> 00:04:21,074
At first that's normal.

167
00:04:21,074 --> 00:04:22,689
But in some people that
swelling can

168
00:04:22,689 --> 00:04:25,477
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

169
00:04:25,477 --> 00:04:27,343
And swollen tissue takes
up more

170
00:04:27,343 --> 00:04:29,309
room than calm tissue
does.

171
00:04:29,309 --> 00:04:30,673
So when you bend,

172
00:04:30,673 --> 00:04:32,208
that tissue gets
compressed.

173
00:04:32,599 --> 00:04:33,772
When you straighten,

174
00:04:33,772 --> 00:04:34,845
it gets pulled tight.

175
00:04:35,347 --> 00:04:36,551
That's the band.

176
00:04:36,551 --> 00:04:38,948
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

177
00:04:38,948 --> 00:04:39,941
And you start being

178
00:04:39,941 --> 00:04:41,074
the one who says,

179
00:04:41,074 --> 00:04:41,937
you go ahead.

180
00:04:41,937 --> 00:04:42,900
I'll stay here.

181
00:04:43,311 --> 00:04:45,146
And that's exactly why so
much

182
00:04:45,146 --> 00:04:47,092
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

183
00:04:47,544 --> 00:04:49,700
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

184
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:50,753
around the knee.

185
00:04:50,753 --> 00:04:51,756
Worth doing,

186
00:04:51,756 --> 00:04:52,749
and I'd done it.

187
00:04:52,749 --> 00:04:54,123
It does nothing about
tissue

188
00:04:54,123 --> 00:04:55,417
taking up room.

189
00:04:55,417 --> 00:04:56,912
A nerve block quiets

190
00:04:56,912 --> 00:04:58,918
the nerve carrying the
signal.

191
00:04:59,429 --> 00:05:01,516
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

192
00:05:01,516 --> 00:05:03,140
But when that irritated
tissue

193
00:05:03,140 --> 00:05:04,755
finally calms down,

194
00:05:04,755 --> 00:05:06,220
it holds less fluid,

195
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:07,473
and it takes up less room.

196
00:05:07,875 --> 00:05:09,229
Less room taken up means

197
00:05:09,229 --> 00:05:11,034
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

198
00:05:11,385 --> 00:05:13,050
That's what takes the
pressure off.

199
00:05:13,552 --> 00:05:15,046
After two years of this,

200
00:05:15,046 --> 00:05:16,450
it finally made sense.

201
00:05:16,992 --> 00:05:18,777
The problem was never the
new knee.

202
00:05:19,209 --> 00:05:20,834
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

203
00:05:21,225 --> 00:05:22,900
He calls it the squeeze.

204
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:25,026
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

205
00:05:25,498 --> 00:05:26,571
I'd bought knee sleeves,

206
00:05:26,571 --> 00:05:28,356
compression braces,
creams,

207
00:05:28,356 --> 00:05:29,891
half of Amazon really,

208
00:05:29,891 --> 00:05:31,686
and all any of it gave me

209
00:05:31,686 --> 00:05:32,629
was an hour.

210
00:05:32,629 --> 00:05:33,542
I even looked at going

211
00:05:33,542 --> 00:05:35,177
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

212
00:05:35,598 --> 00:05:37,393
But at $200 a session

213
00:05:37,393 --> 00:05:39,640
with nothing covered by
insurance,

214
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:40,834
that was a quick no.

215
00:05:41,315 --> 00:05:42,408
Then one night I went

216
00:05:42,408 --> 00:05:43,782
back to that knee
replacement

217
00:05:43,782 --> 00:05:45,738
group and actually read
it.

218
00:05:45,738 --> 00:05:47,092
Thousands of people,

219
00:05:47,092 --> 00:05:48,878
years out from surgery,

220
00:05:48,878 --> 00:05:51,475
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

221
00:05:51,475 --> 00:05:52,679
nobody could explain.

222
00:05:53,191 --> 00:05:54,866
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

223
00:05:54,866 --> 00:05:56,741
the same thing kept coming
up.

224
00:05:57,122 --> 00:05:58,547
This one device,

225
00:05:58,547 --> 00:06:01,014
and people saying it was
the first

226
00:06:01,014 --> 00:06:02,418
thing that made a
difference.

227
00:06:02,418 --> 00:06:04,434
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

228
00:06:04,434 --> 00:06:05,788
alright, here it comes,

229
00:06:05,788 --> 00:06:07,253
he's selling me something,

230
00:06:07,253 --> 00:06:08,808
let me shut that down
right now.

231
00:06:09,159 --> 00:06:11,044
I'm only here because I
made myself

232
00:06:11,044 --> 00:06:13,421
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

233
00:06:13,421 --> 00:06:14,464
that if I ever found

234
00:06:14,464 --> 00:06:15,859
something that helped,

235
00:06:15,859 --> 00:06:16,691
I'd say so.

236
00:06:17,213 --> 00:06:18,908
It's called the KenRelief
Red

237
00:06:18,908 --> 00:06:20,212
Light Therapy Wrap.

238
00:06:20,573 --> 00:06:22,529
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

239
00:06:23,060 --> 00:06:24,414
It looked like the cheap

240
00:06:24,414 --> 00:06:26,501
knee sleeves off Amazon

241
00:06:27,032 --> 00:06:28,517
that did nothing for me.

242
00:06:28,938 --> 00:06:31,235
But I went to their
website anyway,

243
00:06:31,235 --> 00:06:32,398
just to see what all

244
00:06:32,398 --> 00:06:33,421
the fuss was about.

245
00:06:33,993 --> 00:06:35,829
It's the same red light
therapy

246
00:06:35,829 --> 00:06:38,888
clinics charge $200 a
session

247
00:06:38,888 --> 00:06:41,124
for, off machines that
cost

248
00:06:41,124 --> 00:06:42,509
fifty thousand dollars,

249
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:44,244
in a wrap you plug

250
00:06:44,244 --> 00:06:45,377
into the wall at home.

251
00:06:46,059 --> 00:06:47,694
Two hundred and forty
lights.

252
00:06:48,075 --> 00:06:50,412
Red at 660 nanometers

253
00:06:50,412 --> 00:06:52,579
and near-infrared at 850,

254
00:06:52,980 --> 00:06:55,116
run together for the
strongest effect.

255
00:06:55,558 --> 00:06:57,373
Four strength levels.

256
00:06:57,373 --> 00:06:59,209
A five to thirty minute
timer.

257
00:06:59,650 --> 00:07:01,486
Then I saw the guarantee.

258
00:07:01,486 --> 00:07:02,609
Ninety days.

259
00:07:03,010 --> 00:07:04,725
Results or your money
back,

260
00:07:04,725 --> 00:07:07,052
no questions, no store
credit,

261
00:07:07,052 --> 00:07:08,657
and you don't even send it
back.

262
00:07:09,179 --> 00:07:11,546
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

263
00:07:11,546 --> 00:07:12,940
days to change my mind.

264
00:07:13,512 --> 00:07:14,685
There wasn't much to lose,

265
00:07:14,685 --> 00:07:15,708
so I ordered it.

266
00:07:15,708 --> 00:07:16,792
Two of them, actually.

267
00:07:17,153 --> 00:07:18,958
Only the right knee was
replaced,

268
00:07:19,399 --> 00:07:21,466
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

269
00:07:21,466 --> 00:07:23,281
and I'd done it for two
years.

270
00:07:23,943 --> 00:07:26,019
The left one was carrying
the difference.

271
00:07:26,019 --> 00:07:26,601
When it came,

272
00:07:26,601 --> 00:07:28,306
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

273
00:07:28,788 --> 00:07:29,991
because I'd been let down
too

274
00:07:29,991 --> 00:07:31,375
many times to get excited.

275
00:07:31,877 --> 00:07:33,030
What I felt was warmth.

276
00:07:33,482 --> 00:07:34,966
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

277
00:07:35,538 --> 00:07:37,363
More like it was coming
from inside

278
00:07:37,363 --> 00:07:39,299
the knee and spreading
around it.

279
00:07:39,811 --> 00:07:40,874
And that was it.

280
00:07:40,874 --> 00:07:42,569
That was the whole
experience.

281
00:07:42,569 --> 00:07:43,803
When I took it off,

282
00:07:43,803 --> 00:07:44,695
I'll be honest,

283
00:07:44,695 --> 00:07:46,160
nothing dramatic had
happened.

284
00:07:46,621 --> 00:07:48,266
And after what that video
said,

285
00:07:48,266 --> 00:07:50,443
that's exactly what I
expected.

286
00:07:50,443 --> 00:07:51,175
What was different

287
00:07:51,175 --> 00:07:52,148
was that for the first

288
00:07:52,148 --> 00:07:53,251
time in two years

289
00:07:53,251 --> 00:07:54,595
I'd done something for my
knee

290
00:07:54,595 --> 00:07:55,428
instead of to it.

291
00:07:56,089 --> 00:07:57,133
Twenty minutes,

292
00:07:57,133 --> 00:07:58,336
in my own chair.

293
00:07:58,336 --> 00:08:00,372
No drive, no copay.

294
00:08:00,372 --> 00:08:02,188
They say twenty minutes.

295
00:08:02,629 --> 00:08:03,722
I did thirty,

296
00:08:03,722 --> 00:08:04,555
twice a day,

297
00:08:04,996 --> 00:08:06,701
lowest setting that first
week.

298
00:08:07,203 --> 00:08:08,697
I put it on the calendar.

299
00:08:08,697 --> 00:08:09,409
The first week,

300
00:08:09,409 --> 00:08:10,262
I couldn't have told

301
00:08:10,262 --> 00:08:11,666
you if anything was
happening.

302
00:08:12,108 --> 00:08:12,980
I tried not to get

303
00:08:12,980 --> 00:08:13,682
my hopes up.

304
00:08:13,682 --> 00:08:15,076
I'd had things help for a
week

305
00:08:15,076 --> 00:08:15,799
and then stop.

306
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:17,434
But somewhere in the
second week

307
00:08:17,434 --> 00:08:18,517
I noticed I'd come down

308
00:08:18,517 --> 00:08:20,443
the stairs without holding
the rail.

309
00:08:20,443 --> 00:08:21,416
I hadn't decided to.

310
00:08:21,937 --> 00:08:22,940
I just did it,

311
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:24,605
then stopped halfway down

312
00:08:24,605 --> 00:08:25,698
because I realized.

313
00:08:26,090 --> 00:08:27,694
By the end of the fourth
week

314
00:08:27,694 --> 00:08:28,798
I'd slept through the
night

315
00:08:28,798 --> 00:08:30,282
four times running.

316
00:08:30,282 --> 00:08:31,626
I stood at the counter

317
00:08:31,626 --> 00:08:32,880
and finished making dinner

318
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:34,264
without looking for the
stool.

319
00:08:34,826 --> 00:08:36,471
None of that is dramatic.

320
00:08:36,471 --> 00:08:37,444
All of it was gone

321
00:08:37,444 --> 00:08:38,366
for two years.

322
00:08:38,778 --> 00:08:40,413
A few weeks later my wife
asked

323
00:08:40,413 --> 00:08:41,365
if I wanted to walk

324
00:08:41,365 --> 00:08:42,940
the long way around the
block.

325
00:08:43,532 --> 00:08:44,625
And for the first time

326
00:08:44,625 --> 00:08:45,428
in two years,

327
00:08:45,428 --> 00:08:46,380
I said yes.

328
00:08:46,762 --> 00:08:48,637
I wanted to understand
why,

329
00:08:48,637 --> 00:08:49,961
so I read the whole thing.

330
00:08:50,322 --> 00:08:52,057
It comes down to four
steps.

331
00:08:52,057 --> 00:08:52,519
One.

332
00:08:53,030 --> 00:08:54,786
The tissue around a new
knee can

333
00:08:54,786 --> 00:08:57,484
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

334
00:08:58,066 --> 00:08:58,547
Two.

335
00:08:58,988 --> 00:09:01,536
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

336
00:09:01,536 --> 00:09:02,579
so it takes up more

337
00:09:02,579 --> 00:09:03,612
room than it should.

338
00:09:04,053 --> 00:09:04,595
Three.

339
00:09:04,996 --> 00:09:06,681
There's only so much room
in there.

340
00:09:06,681 --> 00:09:08,005
Bending compresses it.

341
00:09:08,527 --> 00:09:09,821
Straightening pulls it
tight.

342
00:09:10,232 --> 00:09:11,787
That's the squeeze.

343
00:09:11,787 --> 00:09:12,308
Four.

344
00:09:12,830 --> 00:09:15,157
Red and near-infrared
light have been

345
00:09:15,157 --> 00:09:17,383
studied for calming that
inflammation,

346
00:09:17,383 --> 00:09:18,728
so the swelling and the
pressure

347
00:09:18,728 --> 00:09:19,731
can come down with it.

348
00:09:20,182 --> 00:09:21,185
In a randomized trial,

349
00:09:21,185 --> 00:09:22,760
patients given light
therapy after

350
00:09:22,760 --> 00:09:23,542
a knee replacement

351
00:09:23,542 --> 00:09:24,294
had less pain,

352
00:09:24,294 --> 00:09:25,257
less swelling

353
00:09:25,257 --> 00:09:26,852
and better early movement
than

354
00:09:26,852 --> 00:09:27,534
those who weren't.

355
00:09:28,126 --> 00:09:30,593
A 2025 review said the
same,

356
00:09:30,593 --> 00:09:31,757
and was clear the evidence

357
00:09:31,757 --> 00:09:32,846
is still limited.

358
00:09:32,846 --> 00:09:34,876
I probably sound like a
broken record

359
00:09:34,876 --> 00:09:36,447
to my crew at the station.

360
00:09:36,447 --> 00:09:38,393
But after two years of
doing everything

361
00:09:38,393 --> 00:09:40,268
I was told and getting
nowhere,

362
00:09:40,268 --> 00:09:41,612
you have no idea what it's

363
00:09:41,612 --> 00:09:43,207
like to sleep through the
night,

364
00:09:43,207 --> 00:09:44,471
say yes to the walk,

365
00:09:44,471 --> 00:09:45,715
and get my life back.

366
00:09:46,176 --> 00:09:47,199
So take it from me.

367
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:48,894
Don't spend another year
waiting

368
00:09:48,894 --> 00:09:49,707
for it to settle.

369
00:09:50,078 --> 00:09:51,462
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

370
00:09:52,064 --> 00:09:53,438
More than ten thousand
people

371
00:09:53,438 --> 00:09:54,581
with pain after a knee

372
00:09:54,581 --> 00:09:57,089
replacement have already
tried this.

373
00:09:57,490 --> 00:09:58,824
Some had it worse than I
did.

374
00:09:59,356 --> 00:10:00,499
You can get the KenRelief

375
00:10:00,499 --> 00:10:02,094
wrap from their website,

376
00:10:02,094 --> 00:10:03,348
with a discount link

377
00:10:03,719 --> 00:10:05,294
and ninety days to try it.

378
00:10:05,785 --> 00:10:07,651
If it doesn't do anything
for you,

379
00:10:07,651 --> 00:10:08,694
you get your money back

380
00:10:08,694 --> 00:10:09,657
and you keep the wrap.

381
00:10:10,088 --> 00:10:11,271
They only release so many

382
00:10:11,271 --> 00:10:12,485
at that price.

383
00:10:12,485 --> 00:10:13,849
If it's still there,

384
00:10:13,849 --> 00:10:14,782
get one,

385
00:10:14,782 --> 00:10:16,333
and stop the squeeze.

